      "writtenOn": "2022-08-24T14:13:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m trying to understand why this is specialized on BUILD_FOR_MAC. My hypothesis is that iOS doesn\u0027t need synchronization because it\u0027s always using shared memory, but Mac might need it because it has dedicated GPUs where synchronizing is actually meaningful.\n\nAre we actually _allowed_ to skip synchronizing resources on iOS/M1 architectures? Or is it just working in practice either way? I feel like it might be safest to just always synchronize (presumably it\u0027s cheap on architectures where it doesn\u0027t matter?)\n\nOr, my initial hypothesis might be off base and there\u0027s a different reason for this. A comment explaining the rationale for future readers would be a good idea.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 545,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 545,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "e5274baf2dc99f936a677ee59c9fea0ff7b9cf37",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1edc7ae6_b468f441",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/mtl/MtlCommandBuffer.mm",
