      "writtenOn": "2022-08-24T17:29:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, that makes sense. However, `SK_BUILD_FOR_MAC` does _not_ mean the same thing, right? AFAIK `SK_BUILD_FOR_MAC` will be true on both M1 Macs and Intel Macs.\n\nWe could (maybe already do?) have something like `SK_BUILD_FOR_APPLE_SILICON` which equates to `SK_BUILD_FOR_IOS || (SK_BUILD_FOR_MAC \u0026\u0026 ARM64)` though? That would let us narrow down the scope of this guard.",
      "parentUuid": "f10459cc_0eab77fe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 545,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 545,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "e5274baf2dc99f936a677ee59c9fea0ff7b9cf37",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
