    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "32b2f9c5_967c25f4",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/mtl/MtlCommandBuffer.mm",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 545,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-24T18:06:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure if we always know at compile time whether we\u0027ll be using Apple silicon or not. The GPU selection itself happens at runtime (even on newer macs) and there is always the possibility (though probably highly uncommon) that a user has a discrete GPU on their modern mac that they prefer to use. We would need to make sure that we ALWAYS select the GPU with unified memory at runtime when running on newer macs if we want to conditionally disable this code on ARM (and maybe that\u0027s what want after all?).\n\nI view the conditional compilation here in somewhat the inverse: `SK_BUILD_FOR_IOS` is an optimization since discrete GPUs there are practically impossible and we are more worried about code size and battery usage. Macs have the possibility of using discrete GPUs and the runtime check based on the GPU type is probably appropriate depending on the GPU the user requested.\n\nAnother thought that I have here is that I think this conditional synchronization should probably be purely based on the actual buffer storage mode and not the GPU type. I imagine we\u0027ll have compute pipelines that operate on intermediate buffers that never have to be synchronized to the CPU (even on discrete GPUs) where `MTLResourceStorageModePrivate` might be preferred. This is sort of what I was trying to achieve with the `BufferType::kXferGpuToCpu` check but I probably misunderstood what that buffer type is for.",
      "parentUuid": "29f423b7_31b5f55b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 545,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 545,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "e5274baf2dc99f936a677ee59c9fea0ff7b9cf37",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
